# Information Security Controls

## Definition

Information Security Controls are safeguards implemented to protect information assets and reduce security risks.

### Objectives

* Prevent Attacks
* Detect Attacks
* Recover from Attacks

---

# Types of Security Controls

```text
Preventive
     ↓
Detective
     ↓
Corrective
```

---

# Preventive Controls

Prevent attacks before they occur.

### Examples

* Firewall
* Antivirus
* Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)
* Access Control
* Strong Password Policies

---

# Detective Controls

Detect attacks when they occur.

### Examples

* Intrusion Detection Systems (IDS)
* Security Monitoring
* Security Logs
* Audit Trails

---

# Corrective Controls

Restore systems after an incident.

### Examples

* Backup Systems
* Disaster Recovery Plans
* Incident Response Plans
* System Restoration

---

# Memory Trick

```text
Lock
 ↓
Camera
 ↓
Repair

Preventive
 ↓
Detective
 ↓
Corrective
```

