# Summary

- Threat is a potential danger.

- Vulnerability is a weakness.

- Risk is the possibility of damage.

- Attack is actual exploitation.

- Security Controls can be Preventive, Detective or Corrective.

- Traditional Hacking Cycle contains 5 phases.
    - Reconnaissance
    - Scanning
    - Gaining Access
    - Maintaining Access
    - Clearing Tracks

- Cyber Kill Chain contains 7 stages.
    - Reconnaissance
    - Weaponization
    - Delivery
    - Exploitation
    - Installation
    - Command & Control
    - Actions on Objectives

- Reconnaissance is the first step of every cyber attack.

